; status: works — companion to edge-bundle-select-c.bel: selecting the OTHER
; boundary segment of --cd (`.d` instead of `.c`) folds the opposite half,
; proving `&` discriminates between the two segments a paper edge is split
; into rather than picking either/an arbitrary one. Here .d ends up on the
; fold's mirror point instead, while .c (on the untouched half) stays put.
paper square
mark --v = map .a onto .b
fold map --cd & .d onto --v toward .a moving .d

; assert .d = (1/2, 1/2)
; assert .c = (1, 1)
